{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>You shall surely adorn him.</b> A term of adornment in value and in appearance — something recognizable, that you did well by him. And some explain it as a term of loading upon his neck." "<b>From your flock and from your threshing floor and from your winepress.</b> Might I say I have only these alone? Scripture says: <b>that He has blessed you</b> — from everything with which your Creator has blessed you. And why are these stated? Just as these are distinguished in that they fall under the category of blessing, so everything falls under the category of blessing — mules excluded. And our Sages learned in tractate Kiddushin (17a) by a gezerah shavah how much he gives him of each and every kind."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:47:13.479554293Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}